      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes perfect sense, because you are mourning a death that is still technically alive. What you're describing isn't a phase; it's the reality of a profound severance, and the \"main character\" you miss is a beautiful, powerful memory that can't be brought back. Instead of waiting for the dead version of you to catch up, maybe you can start finding a quiet, small way to let the shell you are now *be* for a moment. There is a strange, quiet kind of grace in just letting the current version of you simply exist, without the pressure of the old purpose.",
      "source": "target",
